From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blackhat-7 <44942105+blackhat-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:39:06 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 15/33] Conversation cache: a disk tier under the RAM cache
 (--conversation-cache-disk-mib, --conversation-cache-disk-dir)

Ported from opt10/disk-tier (0.1.43) onto 0.2.9 and simplified: a content-addressed blob store
plus one manifest per conversation; evicted conversations, and those still held at exit, are
written in the background and read back when a prompt starts with them, also after a restart.

Changes from the first build:
- the writer works only while the engine is idle (no request and no heartbeat for 1 s, read
  from progress.hpp) and stops between two 1 MiB writes when a request comes in: the PLE table
  is read from the same QLC drive every decode window and writes beside it stall decode
  (r11-plus). This replaces the 256 MiB/s pacing and STRATA_DISK_WRITE_MIB_S.
- one pass per blob (gather, hash, write if missing) instead of hashing everything first.
- one file container for blobs and manifests; one field list for encode and decode.
- the exit flush is bounded (12 s after QUIT, server.py waits 20 s) and runs after the expert
  profile is saved; the most recently used conversation is written first.
- stored conversations are bound to the binary and its STRATA_* environment.
- v0.2.9: a disk match goes the take-whole way (the disk keeps its copy, so siblings lose
  nothing); async park tokens land before an image is queued; the checkpoint clock moves past
  a restored chain's.
- the reader threads of a restore leave the host's CPU.
